    {
      "id": "json-path",
      "kind": "function",
      "name": "jsonPath",
      "parameters": ["Json?", "String", "String"],
      "result": "$type",
      "failures": ["value-absent", "narrowing", "too-large"],
      "note": "The first argument is a Json or Json? value; path and type are string literals, path an RFC 9535 query and type a library scalar term, a collection of them, or Map<String,V> with V a library scalar, which is the result's term. The nodes are graded as a projection wire grades them (contracts/json-projection.json); a map term needs a singular path that selects one object, whose members become the entries, and a node that is no object, a member off V, and a null member into a non-nullable V fail as narrowing, as does a repeated member name anywhere in the source. An empty nodelist gives null for a nullable term that is not a collection, an empty collection for a collection term, and value-absent for another, a non-nullable map term included. A path that takes more than 100000 steps over all its segments (each selector applied to a node, and each value a wildcard or slice passes over), or whose nodes hold more than 16 MiB of JSON, fails as too-large."
